161		/*
162		 * Progressive blur filling the header: eight stacked layers, each with
163		 * a doubling backdrop-filter blur and a mask-image band that slides
164		 * down 12.5% per layer. Stacked, they ramp smoothly from a strong blur
165		 * at the top to no blur by the bottom of the header, instead of the
166		 * hard glass-pane edge a single flat blur gives you. Sized to the
167		 * header's own rendered height (not a hardcoded px) so it always
168		 * matches, regardless of content or breakpoint. Pure CSS, no
169		 * JS/scroll listeners — the browser composites it once.
